  "text": " Do you know, in our circles is millionaire Steve Kirsch, and he's a lot of fun to deal with. He's not a doctor. He's an inventor. He's the guy who invented the optical mouse, and Steve's made a lot of money in his life. Steve has basically said, listen, I'm putting $2 million out on the table right here. Anybody want to come around a table and just get into a roundtable discussion on vaccine safety and efficacy? Let's just have a discussion. We'll film it. Everybody has come to get $2 million, to even discuss vaccine safety and efficacy. That means there's not a single doctor in this country, not a single scientist, not a single official who really thinks the vaccines are safe and efficacious. Why wouldn't they come and make their case and claim $2 million? It would be the easiest $2 million to pull up the table. Isn't that an incredible expression of complicity, of a shameful collusion, and they know they're wrong? That's just basically so listen, anybody in the NIH, the FDA, and CDC, if you think you've done anything right in public policy, I'll pay you $1 million. Just write up a paragraph. Cut $1 million. No one will write a paragraph. Really a paragraph? I mean, it's stunning.",
